cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Reuse Potential for Steel used in Offshore Wind Jacket Foundations"
message: >-
  If you use this software, its results or its figures, please cite it
  using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kenneweg
    given-names: Gregor Elias
    affiliation: University College Cork
abstract: >-
  The fatigue analysis underneath an MEng dissertation on reuse of
  decommissioned offshore wind jacket substructures. A 414-run OpenFAST
  campaign over the OC4 reference jacket carrying the NREL 5MW turbine feeds
  a fatigue post-processing pipeline producing per-member and per-joint
  damage maps, a corrosion trajectory to 25 years, and two can-thickness
  retrofit scenarios for the joints. Members stay well below unity over the
  25-year horizon; splash-zone joints exceed it by more than an order of
  magnitude and remain the worst locations under every scenario examined.
  The downstream reuse-acceptance classification, static/ULS check and
  embodied-carbon comparison from the dissertation are not included in this
  release.
keywords:
  - offshore wind
  - jacket substructure
  - fatigue
  - structural reuse
  - circular economy
  - decommissioning
  - OpenFAST
  - OC4
  - NREL 5MW
  - embodied carbon
